We begin with inspection and a proposed plan only; do not yet produce the full solution. Please proceed in three parts.

(1) INPUT INSPECTION — Open and report on every file under data/: surface_samples.csv (grid extent, resolution, coordinate ranges, energy range/units), curve_samples.csv (number and ordering of corridor samples, coordinates, any monotonic progress along s), tube_scan.csv (transverse scan structure, number of points per sample), kinetic_metric.csv (values, implied reduced-mass/kinetic-energy convention), temperature_grid.csv (min/max, count, whether logarithmic), isotope_cases.csv (case ids, isotopologue labels, longitudinal and transverse mass scales relative to what baseline), and system_manifest.json (units, constants, basin-orientation notes). State any obvious gaps or irregularities (missing values, non-uniform spacing, inconsistent units).

(2) PROPOSED APPROACH — Outline, at the level of equations and algorithm choices, how you plan to compute:
- the per-temperature free-energy profile (how temperature enters, how transverse_frequency_cm1 is derived from the tube scans and converted to a vibrational partition/free-energy contribution, and how the kinetic metric is used);
- the local (geometric) crossing surface vs the optimized crossing location along the corridor (definition of the optimization objective and the flag identifying it);
- the rate estimates log10_k_local, log10_k_optimized, and log10_k_enhanced, including how the enhancement factor and kappa_corridor are defined;
- the transmission/action treatment for both the corridor (1D) and 2D paths, the tunneling method (e.g., WKB/integral-action based) you propose, and how the >=56-row energy grid for transmission_profile.csv is chosen;
- the isotope handling (how longitudinal/transverse mass scales enter the actions and frequencies) and the definition of log10_KIE_sct_vs_light consistent with the light case;
- the crossover_T_K definition and the diagnostics.json contents (conventional-saddle location, crossover temperature, mean 2D-vs-corridor action reduction fraction, rate ordering).

(3) ASSUMPTIONS AND UNCERTAINTIES — List the consequential assumptions you will carry where intent is not stated in the data: e.g., meaning and units of the kinetic metric, the reference mass for the isotopic mass scales and for the light case, the free-energy vs potential-energy convention, the tunneling action normalization, the handling of energies where the relevant basin barrier may not be well defined, and any choices about extrapolation beyond the sampled grid. Keep the plan concrete but do not implement or run the full computation yet; after I review your approach and assumptions I will authorize the main work.

