4) Output plan: vorticity_frames.npy (5,135,135) float32 at frames [0,26,52,78,104] via cell-centered velocities and clamped central differences; kinetic_energy.npy (108,) float32 summing 0.5·dx²·(ū²+v̄²) per frame 0..107.

5) Consequential assumptions/uncertainties to flag: grid indexing conventions (which node is the boundary), how many inner CFL-limited sub-steps are expected per 0.1 frame (depends on max|u|), runtime of the exact Poisson solve × number of steps, and dtype/rounding strategy.

